WEBVTT

00:00:02.260 --> 00:00:04.350
I know who the true culprit is.

00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:07.980
There's really no need to rush,

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:11.490
but I guess I can tell you how 
that will also be resolved.

00:01:49.220 --> 00:01:51.380
You know who the true culprit is?

00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:52.990
What do you mean by that?

00:01:53.330 --> 00:01:59.890
Yes. Frankly speaking, 
you're already out of danger, Muroi-san.

00:01:59.890 --> 00:02:04.040
Even without my help, the likelihood 
that you will be arrested is rather low.

00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:12.150
B-But don't the police have their eyes on me?

00:02:12.450 --> 00:02:14.300
You're just being paranoid.

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:17.060
The police don't have time
to try to go after someone

00:02:17.060 --> 00:02:18.280
who's not even that suspicious.

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:21.530
But why have the suspicions 
around me lessened suddenly?

00:02:22.010 --> 00:02:26.330
The body of the victim, Miharu-san, 
did not have her money, keys,

00:02:26.330 --> 00:02:29.540
identification, or cellphone 
taken from her.

00:02:29.770 --> 00:02:33.000
There are no signs of her 
clothes being disheveled

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:34.900
or anyone entering her apartment.

00:02:35.170 --> 00:02:36.380
That's why.

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:40.590
Miharu-san was dragged to the 
murder scene by the culprit,

00:02:40.590 --> 00:02:43.010
or she was invited there.

00:02:43.630 --> 00:02:45.200
In which case, she and the culprit

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:48.390
would've had time to have 
some degree of conversation.

00:02:48.390 --> 00:02:52.400
And if that's the case, and you were 
the culprit, Miharu-san would've said,

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:55.770
"If you kill me, you'll be caught for sure."

00:02:55.770 --> 00:02:57.690
"If something happens to me,

00:02:57.690 --> 00:03:03.660
I've made sure that a formal accusation 
against you will go to the police."

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:08.650
"If you go home without doing anything 
to me, I won't tell anyone about today."

00:03:08.650 --> 00:03:11.420
Wouldn't she at least try to 
bargain with you like that?

00:03:11.780 --> 00:03:12.860
The accusation could be used

00:03:12.860 --> 00:03:15.750
as a weapon to get revenge against 
the culprit after her death,

00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:19.630
but it could also act as a shield 
so she wouldn't be killed.

00:03:20.140 --> 00:03:23.510
If Miharu-san was truly worried 
about you killing her,

00:03:23.780 --> 00:03:28.010
she would've used the formal accusation 
against you in order to protect herself.

00:03:28.580 --> 00:03:33.270
If that negotiation took place, 
Miharu-san wouldn't have been killed.

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:36.730
There's no way she wouldn't tell 
you about the formal accusation.

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:39.470
After all that,

00:03:39.470 --> 00:03:41.780
if you had killed Miharu-san...

00:03:42.140 --> 00:03:45.140
Even if it was possible that the 
formal accusation was a bluff,

00:03:45.140 --> 00:03:48.910
I would probably think that I'd 
have to deal with it somehow.

00:03:48.910 --> 00:03:49.770
Yes.

00:03:49.770 --> 00:03:51.540
O-Oh...

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:55.170
And in that case, you would try to 
figure out a way to get the letter,

00:03:55.620 --> 00:03:58.490
and probably think of searching 
Miharu-san's apartment.

00:03:59.020 --> 00:04:04.800
But it's possible that you'd show up 
on the security cameras near there.

00:04:05.070 --> 00:04:07.410
And if she had hidden it somewhere else,

00:04:07.410 --> 00:04:11.020
you'd leave traces of your presence 
behind with all that extra movement.

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:14.530
So you'd give up on trying to 
retrieve the letter after all.

00:04:15.070 --> 00:04:16.190
In that case...

00:04:16.190 --> 00:04:19.060
In order to make sure the crime 
didn't seem solely due to a grudge,

00:04:19.060 --> 00:04:23.150
you may have taken her money or other 
belongings to make it look like a robbery,

00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:27.150
or made it seem like it was sexual assault.

00:04:27.690 --> 00:04:31.570
You would've also tried to hide 
the body so it wouldn't be found.

00:04:31.570 --> 00:04:33.750
To ensure she wouldn't 
be identified immediately,

00:04:33.750 --> 00:04:38.210
you'd destroy her teeth and fingerprints, 
and take her ID and her phone.

00:04:38.660 --> 00:04:41.590
You would've at least done these things.

00:04:41.590 --> 00:04:44.360
But there were no signs of any of that,

00:04:44.360 --> 00:04:48.620
and they determined early in the 
investigation that the motive was a grudge.

00:04:49.670 --> 00:04:52.850
And when the police went to question you...

00:04:53.140 --> 00:04:56.100
When they asked you for an alibi, 
you couldn't answer immediately.

00:04:56.100 --> 00:05:00.890
They had security camera footage of 
you and a woman resembling Miharu-san,

00:05:00.890 --> 00:05:03.990
and you weren't able to give a 
clear explanation for that, either.

00:05:04.360 --> 00:05:05.860
How suspicious!

00:05:07.330 --> 00:05:10.820
If you had known about 
Miharu-san's formal accusation,

00:05:10.820 --> 00:05:14.120
you probably would've expected 
to be investigated by the police.

00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:15.570
So it's hard to imagine that

00:05:15.570 --> 00:05:18.920
you'd be unprepared and only do things
that made you seem more suspicious.

00:05:21.050 --> 00:05:23.280
The police have also noticed 
these inconsistencies,

00:05:23.280 --> 00:05:27.380
and are now concentrating on finding 
another with a possible motive.

00:05:27.650 --> 00:05:30.230
If you hadn't met with Yuki-Onna,

00:05:30.230 --> 00:05:32.140
there wouldn't be any 
security camera footage,

00:05:32.540 --> 00:05:36.390
and you could've clearly told them that 
you had no alibi when they questioned you.

00:05:36.750 --> 00:05:39.010
They can't invalidate an 
alibi that doesn't exist,

00:05:39.010 --> 00:05:42.900
and since you're rarely with anyone else, 
there'd be very little evidence against you.

00:05:43.330 --> 00:05:45.930
This would make the police 
investigation more difficult,

00:05:45.930 --> 00:05:48.410
and it would deepen their suspicions.

00:05:50.270 --> 00:05:55.910
Yuki-Onna seemed to be worried that 
she had put you in a predicament,

00:05:55.910 --> 00:05:58.200
but in truth, it was the opposite.

00:05:58.200 --> 00:06:01.710
Ironically, because you couldn't 
talk about Yuki-Onna,

00:06:01.710 --> 00:06:05.510
your suspicious behavior actually 
got you out of danger.

00:06:07.420 --> 00:06:12.730
But then, how would you interpret 
what was written on Miharu's hand?

00:06:13.390 --> 00:06:16.420
You would obviously suspect that 
she was trying to write my name.

00:06:13.390 --> 00:06:17.020
<b>Masayu</b>

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:20.370
It is very likely that Miharu-san 
was killed in a situation

00:06:20.370 --> 00:06:23.210
where she could clearly 
identify who the culprit was.

00:06:23.210 --> 00:06:26.150
If you are not the murderer,

00:06:26.150 --> 00:06:29.910
then it's natural to think 
that the actual murderer

00:06:29.910 --> 00:06:32.180
wrote it on her hand after killing her

00:06:32.180 --> 00:06:34.900
to make it seem like you were the murderer.

00:06:35.740 --> 00:06:37.540
It happens all the time.

00:06:37.540 --> 00:06:39.290
But...

00:06:39.700 --> 00:06:42.660
There's no public knowledge about 
any motive I'd have to kill Miharu.

00:06:43.950 --> 00:06:46.320
Of course, it'd be different 
if people knew that

00:06:46.320 --> 00:06:48.270
I divorced her because 
she tried to kill me,

00:06:48.770 --> 00:06:50.800
but I haven't told anyone.

00:06:51.220 --> 00:06:55.060
And it's not like she'd tell anyone 
that she actually attempted a murder.

00:06:55.310 --> 00:06:59.060
In that case, who would think they 
could set me up as the murderer?

00:06:59.630 --> 00:07:03.490
For some in this world, infidelity is more 
than enough of a motive for murder.

00:07:03.490 --> 00:07:05.510
They may have been 
possessive in a warped way,

00:07:05.510 --> 00:07:07.620
or their pride might've been hurt.

00:07:07.940 --> 00:07:12.320
I'd definitely want to kill my 
boyfriend if he cheated on me.

00:07:12.860 --> 00:07:14.380
<i>I see...</i>

00:07:14.380 --> 00:07:17.830
<i>I was partly at fault for 
Miharu's infidelity, too...</i>

00:07:18.440 --> 00:07:21.830
I don't think your boyfriend would die 
even if you tried to kill him, my lady.

00:07:18.600 --> 00:07:21.180
<i>Though I didn't even think of that.</i>

00:07:22.270 --> 00:07:24.890
If we connect this with the fact that your

00:07:24.890 --> 00:07:27.840
former friend, who had betrayed 
you, died years later,

00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:33.090
it'd be easy to think that you are a vengeful 
man who couldn't condone betrayal.

00:07:33.370 --> 00:07:37.840
Your former colleagues would've also 
feared that you might seek revenge,

00:07:37.840 --> 00:07:41.480
and may have spread such a reputation 
about you without your knowledge.

00:07:41.890 --> 00:07:47.780
That's why the murderer wrote part 
of your name on Miharu-san's hand

00:07:47.780 --> 00:07:50.140
so the suspicions would fall on you.

00:07:51.360 --> 00:07:55.190
And in order to make the police 
believe that you are the murderer,

00:07:55.190 --> 00:07:59.110
it would be vital for you to not have 
an alibi at the time of the murder.

00:08:01.410 --> 00:08:05.380
So the murderer would've made 
sure you didn't have an alibi,

00:08:03.540 --> 00:08:06.700
<i>We're getting closer to the truth.</i>

00:08:05.380 --> 00:08:09.300
or confirmed that there were no witnesses.

00:08:09.750 --> 00:08:14.300
The person who was able to do that, 
and <i>did</i> do that, is the true murderer.

00:08:10.680 --> 00:08:14.300
<i>Perhaps I shouldn't let her say any more.</i>

00:08:14.300 --> 00:08:17.000
Muroi-san, in your case, there are only

00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:19.490
a few people who could 
have done this, correct?

00:08:19.490 --> 00:08:21.810
<i>There's only one person</i>

00:08:22.470 --> 00:08:23.840
<i>who could've done that.</i>

00:08:26.410 --> 00:08:29.070
Are you telling me... it was Iizuka?

00:08:29.750 --> 00:08:30.470
Yes.

00:08:31.830 --> 00:08:35.470
Iizuka Nagisa. She is the murderer.

00:08:34.030 --> 00:08:36.450
Iizuka Nagisa

00:08:34.300 --> 00:08:36.450
Decline                    Answer

00:08:36.450 --> 00:08:38.450
Iizuka Nagisa

00:08:51.270 --> 00:08:55.970
<b>The Yuki-Onna's Innocence</b>

00:08:55.970 --> 00:08:58.220
Iizuka Nagisa

00:08:55.970 --> 00:08:58.220
Decline                         Answer

00:09:06.530 --> 00:09:07.900
Masayuki...

00:09:10.360 --> 00:09:12.860
I've at least mentioned her to you.

00:09:13.400 --> 00:09:16.110
When my company went through a merger,

00:09:16.110 --> 00:09:18.050
Iizuka sided with me.

00:09:18.050 --> 00:09:20.110
She was one of the few employees we had,

00:09:20.450 --> 00:09:25.570
and a capable subordinate who could carry 
on the work I'd started before quitting.

00:09:26.780 --> 00:09:29.040
She was the only one who 
kept in contact with me

00:09:29.040 --> 00:09:31.250
after I was run out of my company.

00:09:31.580 --> 00:09:34.030
I thought she was just being cordial,

00:09:34.030 --> 00:09:36.540
but I didn't think she 
had a grudge against me.

00:09:37.650 --> 00:09:40.080
On that night around 7 PM...

00:09:40.080 --> 00:09:43.020
Yuki-Onna had come over, 
so we were preparing tempura,

00:09:43.020 --> 00:09:45.520
Iizuka Nagisa

00:09:43.380 --> 00:09:44.710
and then I got a phone call.

00:09:48.610 --> 00:09:49.370
Hello?

00:09:49.990 --> 00:09:51.740
<i>Are you alone right now?</i>

00:09:53.740 --> 00:09:55.490
You can go ahead and eat.

00:09:55.800 --> 00:09:56.530
Right now?

00:09:57.220 --> 00:09:58.780
I'm home alone.

00:09:59.630 --> 00:10:00.860
It's so good!

00:10:01.250 --> 00:10:03.150
I've just been a shut-in, as usual.

00:10:03.540 --> 00:10:04.810
<i>I see.</i>

00:10:05.300 --> 00:10:08.540
I'm planning on having a drink 
and reading until dawn.

00:10:08.540 --> 00:10:09.700
President...

00:10:09.700 --> 00:10:11.250
<i>I'm not the president anymore.</i>

00:10:11.710 --> 00:10:14.680
Please excuse me. Muroi-san...

00:10:14.680 --> 00:10:15.830
<i>What is it?</i>

00:10:15.830 --> 00:10:20.430
I'll be waiting for you to start a new job.

00:10:20.950 --> 00:10:21.650
Right...

00:10:22.350 --> 00:10:25.260
Well, I'm gonna hang up. 
I'll leave the rest to you.

00:10:25.260 --> 00:10:27.470
<i>Right. Goodnight.</i>

00:10:49.140 --> 00:10:54.420
And after she confirmed you wouldn't have 
a solid alibi at the time of the murder,

00:10:54.420 --> 00:10:57.270
she set her murder plans in motion.

00:10:57.270 --> 00:11:00.300
B-But why would Iizuka...

00:11:00.640 --> 00:11:02.610
I don't know why she'd 
have a grudge against me,

00:11:02.610 --> 00:11:06.060
and she only met Miharu a handful of times.

00:11:06.060 --> 00:11:09.690
She had been calling me quite often lately.

00:11:06.410 --> 00:11:09.690
Call History
All
Iizuka Nagisa                            Yesterday
Safe Care Damage Insurance     Tuesday
Iizuka Nagisa                            Thursday
Withheld                                  Friday
Iizuka Nagisa                            Sunday
Takumo Home Center               Wednesday
Iizuka Nagisa                            Saturday
Iizuka Nagisa                            Saturday

00:11:10.080 --> 00:11:14.220
She said she learned of Miharu's murder 
because the police came to question her.

00:11:14.820 --> 00:11:19.820
She wanted to know if she could help 
with anything, and if she could...

00:11:20.330 --> 00:11:21.720
come over sometime.

00:11:22.510 --> 00:11:23.570
Message

00:11:22.510 --> 00:11:23.570
Iizuka: Muroi-san

00:11:23.570 --> 00:11:25.370
<b>Message</b>

00:11:23.570 --> 00:11:25.370
<b>Iizuka: Muroi-san</b>

00:11:25.370 --> 00:11:26.830
<b>Message</b>

00:11:25.370 --> 00:11:26.830
<b>Iizuka: Please call me</b>

00:11:27.130 --> 00:11:29.350
She tried to frame me?

00:11:29.790 --> 00:11:31.330
But why?!

00:11:33.830 --> 00:11:36.290
Well, I'm afraid I don't 
have all the answers.

00:11:37.710 --> 00:11:39.250
The police are now

00:11:39.250 --> 00:11:42.800
investigating under the assumption 
that someone tried to frame you,

00:11:43.090 --> 00:11:44.920
so let's wait until she's arrested.

00:11:46.710 --> 00:11:51.500
She probably didn't think that she 
was the only one who could've known

00:11:51.500 --> 00:11:53.310
what you were doing that night.

00:11:53.930 --> 00:11:56.720
She probably didn't think 
that you were so satisfied

00:11:56.720 --> 00:11:59.570
with your relationship with 
Yuki-Onna that you had

00:11:59.570 --> 00:12:02.200
completely separated yourself 
from the rest of society.

00:12:02.740 --> 00:12:04.680
And since she let her guard down so much,

00:12:04.680 --> 00:12:06.970
she might be arrested sooner than we think.

00:12:09.800 --> 00:12:11.460
Be strong.

00:12:11.960 --> 00:12:14.200
You didn't do anything wrong.

00:12:15.420 --> 00:12:16.270
Yeah.

00:12:17.320 --> 00:12:18.730
I'll make it through this.

00:12:19.550 --> 00:12:21.630
Even if I am at fault...

00:12:23.000 --> 00:12:29.100
You told me that false theory first 
so that I could handle the truth.

00:12:29.410 --> 00:12:34.980
Without that, you knew I might never 
be able to trust another soul again.

00:12:35.370 --> 00:12:37.460
I am the goddess of wisdom, after all.

00:12:37.460 --> 00:12:39.360
I am always thoughtful.

00:12:39.360 --> 00:12:43.470
But I'm surprised you can predict where 
the police are in their investigation.

00:12:43.830 --> 00:12:46.030
Is that due to your insight as 
the goddess of wisdom, too?

00:12:46.330 --> 00:12:51.120
I just had some ghosts eavesdrop on how 
their investigation was going at the station.

00:12:51.380 --> 00:12:55.750
That's also how I found out that they 
were no longer as suspicious of you.

00:12:56.100 --> 00:12:58.310
Isn't that cheating?

00:12:58.310 --> 00:13:00.500
Well, doesn't that speed up the process?

00:13:00.810 --> 00:13:05.210
There were quite a few ghosts at the 
riverbed where the murder happened,

00:13:05.210 --> 00:13:07.380
and they witnessed it.

00:13:07.890 --> 00:13:08.890
Female.

00:13:08.890 --> 00:13:11.140
About 155 centimeters tall.

00:13:11.140 --> 00:13:12.390
Brown hair.

00:13:12.390 --> 00:13:14.660
From their testimonies,

00:13:14.660 --> 00:13:17.600
I knew some physical details and 
the sex of the murderer,

00:13:17.600 --> 00:13:20.150
and it was clear that you 
were not the culprit.

00:13:21.190 --> 00:13:25.280
They also witnessed the murderer 
writing the message on her hand.

00:13:25.280 --> 00:13:28.280
<b>Masayu</b>

00:13:25.280 --> 00:13:28.280
So I narrowed down the 
list of people around you,

00:13:28.550 --> 00:13:33.310
and had the ghosts who witnessed the 
murder confirm that it was Iizuka Nagisa.

00:13:33.930 --> 00:13:35.790
So you knew who the murderer was

00:13:36.140 --> 00:13:38.190
before you even came up with that theory?

00:13:38.190 --> 00:13:41.290
I clearly mentioned that I 
knew who the true culprit was.

00:13:41.740 --> 00:13:44.550
I won't interfere with whatever 
you're going to do now.

00:13:44.850 --> 00:13:48.190
Whether it be with this incident or 
your relationship with Yuki-Onna.

00:13:48.950 --> 00:13:51.380
There are differences 
between humans and yokai,

00:13:51.380 --> 00:13:53.410
so things won't go well forever.

00:13:54.140 --> 00:13:57.060
But still, there is a honeymoon period.

00:13:58.050 --> 00:13:59.810
And even if it may be short,

00:13:59.810 --> 00:14:03.690
I'm pretty sure no one can 
take that away from you.

00:14:04.390 --> 00:14:05.980
I wish you both happiness.

00:14:14.890 --> 00:14:16.540
Masayuki!

00:14:17.240 --> 00:14:20.330
Did you hear that? Our ladyship approves!

00:14:21.790 --> 00:14:22.470
Yeah.

00:14:27.610 --> 00:14:30.310
But don't forget the contraceptives!

00:14:30.310 --> 00:14:32.280
Unlike in the past, I'm sure a child

00:14:32.280 --> 00:14:34.980
born between a human and yokai 
would struggle in the modern day.

00:14:35.330 --> 00:14:39.170
In Koizumi Yakumo's story, 
the Yuki-Onna had ten children—

00:14:39.170 --> 00:14:40.940
You're really going to bring that up?

00:14:42.130 --> 00:14:43.730
Oh, whoa.

00:14:46.840 --> 00:14:49.860
What are you doing, Senpai?

00:14:49.860 --> 00:14:52.870
I dropped the tea, and...

00:14:53.180 --> 00:14:55.240
Um, uh...

00:14:55.670 --> 00:14:56.750
Good evening?

00:15:01.940 --> 00:15:02.830
Pardon.

00:15:02.830 --> 00:15:05.640
This is my boyfriend, Sakuragawa Kuro.

00:15:05.640 --> 00:15:12.010
He's part yokai, and to Yuki-Onna, 
he probably looks like some terrible monster.

00:15:12.010 --> 00:15:13.500
Monster...

00:15:13.500 --> 00:15:15.350
H-He...

00:15:15.350 --> 00:15:19.940
He ate the flesh of a mermaid and 
also the flesh of another yokai,

00:15:19.940 --> 00:15:23.310
and became a monster with terrible powers!

00:15:25.140 --> 00:15:27.070
I can't say he really looks like that.

00:15:27.570 --> 00:15:29.820
He's got a much cuter face than I do.

00:15:29.820 --> 00:15:33.570
Nay! In my eyes, he's...

00:15:34.020 --> 00:15:35.540
That creature is...

00:15:41.570 --> 00:15:45.460
In comparison, you are so precious!

00:15:45.460 --> 00:15:46.460
Precious?

00:15:46.940 --> 00:15:51.290
I knew I smelled something rancid 
and felt an ominous presence.

00:15:51.290 --> 00:15:55.470
Er, I know that Kuro-dono 
means no harm, but...

00:15:55.470 --> 00:16:00.980
A-Anyway, my lady, 
how can I ever thank you?

00:16:00.980 --> 00:16:04.950
Oh, it's fine, really. 
You two are in the optimal mood.

00:16:04.950 --> 00:16:06.230
So hurry on home

00:16:06.230 --> 00:16:08.200
and bone already.

00:16:08.200 --> 00:16:09.380
That's so vulgar...

00:16:09.380 --> 00:16:10.490
Hey!

00:16:12.530 --> 00:16:15.280
With that, my lady and Kuro-dono,

00:16:15.630 --> 00:16:18.220
thank you so much!

00:16:19.630 --> 00:16:22.410
Well, that was another troublesome case.

00:16:22.830 --> 00:16:26.110
It would've been easy for you 
to just identify the murderer.

00:16:26.510 --> 00:16:31.260
Considering Yuki-Onna's reaction, it was 
the right decision to have you hide.

00:16:32.900 --> 00:16:36.990
For this case, it was necessary 
for Yuki-Onna to defend Muroi-san.

00:16:38.260 --> 00:16:41.330
Yokai have a hard time defying me as it is,

00:16:41.330 --> 00:16:42.890
but if you were also present,

00:16:42.890 --> 00:16:46.950
Yuki-Onna likely would've shriveled 
up and been unable to speak.

00:16:46.950 --> 00:16:50.570
Then you probably went too far with 
that act in the beginning, didn't you?

00:16:51.320 --> 00:16:53.340
That alone nearly made her shrivel up.

00:16:53.950 --> 00:16:56.870
Well, just imagining that was infuriating.

00:16:56.870 --> 00:16:59.700
It's because of how you usually act, Senpai.

00:17:00.150 --> 00:17:03.930
Well, I have no choice but to tag along

00:17:04.210 --> 00:17:07.460
because you're always taking on 
more than you can handle.

00:17:10.580 --> 00:17:13.790
I wrote out an outline and 
gathered some documents,

00:17:13.790 --> 00:17:15.290
so make sure you write that report.

00:17:21.300 --> 00:17:25.850
So... what was the motive of the 
true murderer, Iizuka Nagisa?

00:17:26.170 --> 00:17:27.590
You already looked into that, right?

00:17:28.030 --> 00:17:32.110
She respects Muroi-san, and also loves him.

00:17:32.440 --> 00:17:37.490
That's why she was frustrated 
that his ex-wife cheated on him.

00:17:38.310 --> 00:17:41.870
She also wanted to go with Muroi-san 
when he left the company, but...

00:17:42.790 --> 00:17:47.100
I'll be able to quit without 
worrying if you remain here.

00:17:47.100 --> 00:17:52.500
Muroi-san had no intention of finding 
a new job nor relying on her.

00:17:53.090 --> 00:17:54.730
She resisted getting close to him

00:17:54.730 --> 00:17:56.990
because she figured she'd 
just be inconveniencing him.

00:17:56.990 --> 00:18:00.930
But his distrust for others 
had him at a standstill.

00:18:01.260 --> 00:18:04.610
No matter how many months passed, 
he just stayed cooped up in that house.

00:18:04.020 --> 00:18:06.270
Flower Gift Promotion

00:18:05.020 --> 00:18:06.850
She just couldn't bear that any longer,

00:18:06.850 --> 00:18:10.020
and resorted to murder to 
get out of that situation.

00:18:10.580 --> 00:18:12.650
Iizuka Nagisa pretended like she just

00:18:12.650 --> 00:18:15.860
coincidentally ran into Miharu-san 
while on a business trip.

00:18:16.400 --> 00:18:21.910
By the way, Muroi-san was asking me 
if I knew what you were up to lately.

00:18:22.250 --> 00:18:25.480
He might be thinking about reconciling.

00:18:25.910 --> 00:18:26.820
What?

00:18:27.300 --> 00:18:31.580
Her plan was to start chatting with Miharu-san 
even more, after bringing up Muroi-san,

00:18:31.580 --> 00:18:34.670
and then taking her somewhere 
with no one else around,

00:18:34.910 --> 00:18:38.640
but Miharu-san was scared that 
her ex-husband would harm her,

00:18:38.640 --> 00:18:41.430
so she was genuinely curious 
as to what he was up to.

00:18:44.020 --> 00:18:46.460
She wanted to know more, so apparently,

00:18:46.460 --> 00:18:49.320
it was Miharu-san who 
invited her to the riverbed.

00:18:51.340 --> 00:18:54.090
Iizuka Nagisa couldn't have 
asked for a better scenario.

00:19:02.420 --> 00:19:06.040
And then, Miharu-san was killed.

00:19:08.220 --> 00:19:10.380
But why did Iizuka Nagisa go

00:19:10.380 --> 00:19:13.840
out of her way to make it look like 
Muroi-san committed the murder?

00:19:14.090 --> 00:19:16.630
If she was obsessed with him and loved him,

00:19:16.630 --> 00:19:19.580
she may have killed Miharu-san, 
but not resorted to framing him.

00:19:19.580 --> 00:19:21.720
Well, that's the twisted part, you see.

00:19:22.580 --> 00:19:24.520
She had kept in contact 
with him after he quit,

00:19:24.520 --> 00:19:28.420
and even if he was treated like a 
murderer, if she believed in him

00:19:28.420 --> 00:19:30.540
and didn't change her attitude toward him,

00:19:30.540 --> 00:19:33.120
you'd think Muroi-san would 
end up relying on her.

00:19:33.770 --> 00:19:37.080
He may even eventually fall in love with her.

00:19:37.660 --> 00:19:39.620
After being suspected of murder,

00:19:39.620 --> 00:19:42.200
Muroi-san would be suffering 
and feel all alone,

00:19:42.200 --> 00:19:43.960
and only she would get closer to him,

00:19:43.960 --> 00:19:46.360
believe in him, and devote herself to him.

00:19:46.360 --> 00:19:48.930
That's the kind of situation 
she was trying to create.

00:19:52.000 --> 00:19:55.950
That's why the murder victim 
could've been anyone

00:19:55.950 --> 00:19:59.270
who would make Muroi-san a suspect,

00:19:59.270 --> 00:20:01.510
but not make Iizuka Nagisa a suspect.

00:20:01.510 --> 00:20:03.510
Yeah, that's twisted, all right.

00:20:04.180 --> 00:20:07.930
But if Muroi-san ended up getting 
arrested as the murderer,

00:20:07.930 --> 00:20:09.750
what good would that have done?

00:20:10.110 --> 00:20:13.520
That would probably be the part 
Iizuka Nagisa miscalculated.

00:20:14.250 --> 00:20:17.270
And trying to make others believe 
Muroi-san couldn't forgive his ex-wife

00:20:17.520 --> 00:20:20.810
for having cheated on him and ultimately 
killed her is rather forced.

00:20:21.270 --> 00:20:24.910
The message she wrote and her knowledge 
of evidence were both weak.

00:20:25.260 --> 00:20:27.690
So even if Muroi-san was suspected of murder,

00:20:27.690 --> 00:20:32.020
she probably thought they wouldn't be able 
to make that suspicion stick in the end.

00:20:33.220 --> 00:20:36.560
But then, Miharu-san's formal 
accusation letter was revealed,

00:20:36.560 --> 00:20:39.150
and there was footage that 
made him even more suspicious.

00:20:39.510 --> 00:20:44.250
And because of that, the police suspected 
Muroi-san way more than necessary,

00:20:44.250 --> 00:20:46.930
so he was actually almost arrested.

00:20:46.930 --> 00:20:48.300
I see.

00:20:48.820 --> 00:20:53.290
So that's why, even two weeks 
after the murder was discovered,

00:20:53.290 --> 00:20:56.060
she didn't create more evidence 
that would put Muroi-san

00:20:56.060 --> 00:20:57.650
at a further disadvantage.

00:20:58.120 --> 00:21:02.440
I wasn't sure if I should've 
told Muroi-san all this earlier,

00:21:03.030 --> 00:21:06.470
but she probably couldn't go through with it.

00:21:06.900 --> 00:21:08.830
It would just make him depressed again.

00:21:09.780 --> 00:21:14.330
It'll take a while for the police 
to uncover the truth,

00:21:14.620 --> 00:21:15.880
and by then,

00:21:15.880 --> 00:21:19.220
I'm sure Muroi-san will have healed 
enough to accept everything.

00:21:20.290 --> 00:21:25.290
Tonight, Yuki-Onna has the opportunity 
to get even closer to him.

00:21:25.710 --> 00:21:28.970
If I were to tell him something 
that would've interrupted that,

00:21:28.970 --> 00:21:30.910
Yuki-Onna would resent me.

00:21:31.590 --> 00:21:34.980
Muroi-san might be fated to 
have bad luck with women.

00:21:35.790 --> 00:21:38.750
When his friend first tried to kill him,

00:21:38.750 --> 00:21:41.730
when his ex-wife attempted to murder him,

00:21:42.070 --> 00:21:46.760
and then this incident all involved 
some kind of trouble with women.

00:21:47.190 --> 00:21:50.700
He's probably destined to have 
wicked women fall in love with him.

00:21:51.160 --> 00:21:53.410
I mean, there's Yuki-Onna, too.

00:21:53.750 --> 00:21:55.940
In the end, she's a yokai.

00:21:55.940 --> 00:21:59.130
Yuki-Onna is very emotional 
and quite beautiful,

00:21:59.130 --> 00:22:02.040
but one wrong step, and she 
could freeze him to death.

00:22:02.380 --> 00:22:06.010
<b>Man Found
Frozen
to Death
in His
Own Home!</b>

00:22:02.380 --> 00:22:06.010
Muroi-san when he was discovered

00:22:02.380 --> 00:22:06.020
In the future, I wouldn't be 
surprised to see an article saying

00:22:06.020 --> 00:22:07.550
that Muroi-san froze to death.

00:22:08.940 --> 00:22:10.380
Wait.

00:22:11.240 --> 00:22:13.600
I can totally relate to the guy.

00:22:15.100 --> 00:22:20.730
Yes, well, your ex-girlfriend and 
Rikka-san were quite problematic.

00:22:20.980 --> 00:22:23.880
I'd say you're the most problematic.

00:22:23.880 --> 00:22:26.990
How rude! What would make 
you say such a thing?

00:22:26.990 --> 00:22:30.490
I told you! 
Wasn't our ladyship quite amazing?

00:22:30.730 --> 00:22:32.580
She's a bit vulgar, though.

00:22:32.580 --> 00:22:33.490
Hey.

00:22:34.260 --> 00:22:38.410
<i>It's not like my relationship with 
her is going to last forever.</i>

00:22:38.740 --> 00:22:40.750
<i>Our values and our lifespan are different.</i>

00:22:41.290 --> 00:22:44.290
<i>Letting her be seen will also 
probably cause problems.</i>

00:22:45.420 --> 00:22:49.880
<i>But still, I'd like for our time 
together to continue a little longer.</i>

00:22:52.140 --> 00:22:54.740
Hm? What is it?

00:22:55.490 --> 00:22:56.890
Nothing.

00:23:06.940 --> 00:23:09.970
To be continued
